Z||000019||88formula||01-10-2001||05:37 PM||||The Northstar engine is 4.6-liters.||||reg||1
Z||000020||lou_dias||01-11-2001||08:05 AM||||I know it's a 4.6 V8, but if you follow the technology of TDOC engines from GM, it goes:<P>quad 4 (2.2-2.4L 150-180hp)<BR>quad 6 (3.4 TDOC 210-220hp)<BR>LT5 (5.7L 360-405hp 32 valve v8 in ZR1 vettes)<BR>then Northstar (4.6 v8 275-300 hp)<BR>and back to 3.5L v6(Shortstar 215hp)<BR>I'm not sure what the layout of the 3.5 is.  Is it a 60 or 90 degree engine?||||reg||1
Z||000021||MooCow||01-11-2001||11:18 AM||||According to Ed Parks the 3.5 is a Grooms remanufactured 3.4 (now 3.5-3.6) is $2175. I was going to get that but don't have the funds.  <BR>        Hey jerpro when I get back and on one of these days when the weather is nice I could go to GR and give you  ride an a 3.4 from Ed Parks.  I am only about 45 minutes away.  Let me know.<P>                           Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000022||lou_dias||01-11-2001||12:28 PM||||the 3.5 I was talking about is the new TDOC 3.5 that GM came out with this year.<P>I have a Grooms 3.5 pushrod from Ed myself.  It was put into my GT in May.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Will||01-11-2001||03:35 PM||||I think you mean "TDC" not "TDOC". TDC means "twin dual cam". I have only heard that applied to the 3.4 TDC. Every other engine on earth that uses two cam shafts on top of the cylinder head is called DOHC or Dual Overhead Cam<P>The 3.5 Shortstar is a 90 degree V6.<P>Check out all of GM's engines except the Aurora V8 at <A HREF="http://www.gmpowertrain.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpowertrain.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||lou_dias||01-12-2001||09:31 AM||||TDOC has 4 cams<BR>a dohc has 2 cam<P>the 3.4 is a tdoc (tdohc, samething, more letters)||||reg||1
